+The core gradient computation relies on the differentiable alpha-compositing equation provided in the parent article [Gradient Computation and Back-Propagation](10202-gradient-computation-and-back-propagation.md) [S1, unofficial]. The gradient of the loss $L$ with respect to the parameters $\theta_k$ of the $k$-th Gaussian is computed via the chain rule [G]:
 $$
